==[[Toon of the Week]] Quests==
{{TOTWQuests|Encounter {{CI|Twisted Sprout|name=true}} 3 times.|Complete [[Floor]] 10 as Sprout or with at least 1 Sprout in your run.|Activate the {{TI|Savory Charm|name=true}} [[Trinket]] on [[Floor]] 10 or higher.}}

===Rewards===
*1 Quest completed: {{AT|Sprout Fan}} [[Title]]
*2 Quests completed: {{SI|Golden Sprout!|name=true}} [[Sticker]]
*3 Quests completed: {{Skin|Golden Berry|toon=Sprout}} [[Skin]]

===Strategies===
*Play until you reach [[Floor]] 5 then restart multiple times or try to get as far as you can until you encounter {{CI|Twisted Sprout|name=true}} 3 times in a single run. This is easier by doing an organized Run or on days where Twisted Sprout is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].
*You don't have to play as Sprout in order to do this quest. As long as you have at least one Sprout on your team, and complete [[Floor]] 10, you should be able to do it. This may be easier with other healer Toons, as Sprout cannot heal himself with his Ability.
*You don't have to play as Sprout in order to do this quest. As long as you have the {{TI|Savory Charm|name=true}} equipped, and activate it when you reach [[Floor]] 10, you should be able to do it. Try to stock up on [[Health|Healing]] [[Items]] or play as {{CI|Teagan|name=true}} to ensure you don't get to one heart before Floor 10.

==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, have a Distractor [[Toon]] bring {{CI|Twisted Sprout|name=true}} to the elevator or seek him out so you can get 5% aggro Research. Playing as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} also helps getting Research faster because of his Passive [[Ability]]. This will be easier if Twisted Sprout is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].
*For the third requirement, play as {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} and try to complete his [[Mastery]] Quests by going on multiple runs. It is recommended to go on an organized Run or do specific quests in certain runs.

==Strategies==
Sprout is a great supporter and a superb [[Toon]] for many types of runs. His mobility is above average: with 4{{Star}} Movement Speed and 5 Star Stamina, the highest in the game tied with {{CI|Blot|name=true}}. Sprout makes for a very capable distractor. The only real downside to playing Sprout is his low Extractability (2 Stars for both Extraction Speed and Skill Check), but this can be mitigated with [[Trinkets]] such as {{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}} or {{TI|Stress Ball|name=true}}.

If you have other distractors in your lobby, such as {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} or {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}, it's suggested to allow them to fill up that role instead. The reason Sprout's utility overshadows his use as a distractor is his Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Sprout|name=true}}, which allows Sprout to heal any other hurt Toon in range for 1{{Heart}} at the cost of 100 {{Tape|name=true}}. It can still complement his role as a distractor by also allowing him to heal Toons in an emergency situation. This will be a lifesaver for your teammates. So, while distracting is a great use of Sprout's talents, scavenging for Tapes and [[Items]] instead is very helpful to heal other players in your team. Additionally, if a {{CI|Bassie|name=true}} is in the team, she can help Sprout search for Items before dropping them with her Ability. This makes Sprout better-applied as a backup distractor than the main one despite his excellent stats. He can still contribute outside of distracting by extracting [[Treadmill Machines]] rather efficiently and working with others on Duo Machines.

Since Tapes may be hard to come by, it's suggested to prioritize healing distractors, healers, and Toons on one heart—otherwise, save around 200 Tapes for emergencies unless the [[Floor]] is particularly dangerous and you're concerned for your teammates. Having multiple Sprouts in the same run is inefficient, as the Ability cost increases by 50 Tapes per Sprout in your party. Additionally, there is a global healing cooldown of 30s that will interfere with other Sprouts' gameplay.

Do note that his Ability is not the most efficient method of Healing. Healing Items like {{II|Health Kit|name=true|plural=a}} can heal for Sprout at the same price or less, and {{II|Bandage|name=false}}s for nearly half. Due to Sprout's value, try to save some Tapes in case a Bandage appears in [[Dandy's Elevator Shop]], since if one does, your teammates will also have a chance to buy it, making the loss of Tapes less risky. Having enough Tapes at all times for a possible heal in Dandy's Shop or to heal someone else is important. Because of this, it may be wise to ensure that other players have around 80 Tapes at the beginning of a run before Sprout takes them all, so that all players would be able to buy any heals or useful Items that come along. As Sprout cannot heal himself without bandages/health kits or a {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} present, it's understandable to pursue any type of healing he can get.

Sprout works well with Cosmo, as the latter's higher Stealth stat + shorter cooldown can allow him to deliver Hearts more easily to those in peril. Sprout can 'reimburse' him for any Hearts lost, and he can in turn give Hearts to Sprout, making their teamwork very effective. If {{CI|Teagan|name=true}} is in the party it allows Sprout to have one less Toon to worry about, making resources easier to manage for the others, but Tape division could be a hurdle. This may not be a huge issue though, considering Teagan only needs 75 Tapes to heal herself, which is just 15 more than a Bandage.

Another great pairing is Sprout and {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}. Cocoa can drop BonBons for Sprout, which is equivalent to 5 Tapes, essentially giving 5 Tapes every 21.8-40 seconds depending on the Trinkets and Cards. Even though this isn't extremely effective, it can be very helpful if other teammates are taking Tapes and not letting you do the Machines.

Sprout's pairing with Bassie is also an excellent option. Bassie's ability to drop items can help Sprout gain Tapes more efficiently, especially if she buys more common Items from Dandy's Shop, practically buying Tapes for him. However, if Bassie's inventory is filled with rare items or healing items on later Floors, it is not a reliable option for long runs. Nonetheless, it can be a good boost early on.

Sprout can also make a good team with {{CI|Yatta|name=true}} as she can drop Items from completing Machines for Sprout to use for Tapes. This strategy reaches its full potential with rarer drops like {{II|Jawbreaker|name=false}}s or in smaller runs where less people take the dropped Items. It allows an infinite supply of Tapes, as long as the Yatta completes Machines. She also drops more Items when being hit, but it is discouraged to ask them to get hit so you can earn more Tapes, unless they wish to use up a heal. Although the {{II|Box o' Chocolates|name=false}} she drops can also be used to earn 8 Tapes, it is recommended to leave them for your team due to Sprout's already high mobility.

Sprout's Passive Ability, '''Overprotective''', shows you how many hearts a Toon has and where each of them are. This is great for locating injured Toons and determining which of them need healing the most. However, this can be used for more than tracking hearts.
#'''Optimizing routes.''' While distracting, it can be used to change your route on a dime without running as much risk of running into teammates. It will also let you know if any damaged teammates are drawing near so you can initiate emergency maneuvers ahead of time. This can help you roam and collect Tapes while distracting (though caution should still be taken).
#'''Tracking Movement for clues.''' Noticing if a certain heart keeps running in circles or is stagnating in a specific location can clue you in that, that Toon is either distracting a [[Twisted]] in the former's case or could be working on a Machine for the latter. If there's no backup distractor and you notice a teammate has been distracting for a while, it could be a good idea to run over and relieve them. This can also help you identify those who are AFK.
#'''Seeing how many people are at the [[Elevator]].''' Sprout excels at finishing the last Machine even at a distance due to this trait and his superior Movement Stats. It only takes a quick glance to see if most Toons have made it, which has the potential to save you from popping the Machine too early and a chance to put them in danger. If you notice Hearts that are very far from the Elevator, ensure they're okay before initiating [[Panic Mode]].
#'''Monitoring individuals.''' Since a different graphic is used when at full Hearts, partial Health, and one Heart, respectively, if only one of your teammates is at a certain Heart level it's possible to track them specifically. The best use cases for this tactic are when {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}} is in your party, a Looey at one heart is distracting, or your party is very small, but despite being a niche tool, this advantage can be helpful.
#'''Reporting danger.''' If a teammate dies or is critically injured, a keen-eyed Sprout might be the first to realize who and where it was. Using clues from tracking Movement and individual monitoring, it can easily become evident if a distractor dies or switches locations. This information can be crucial and is not always reported, so do your best to keep your team updated. Letting any Cosmos or Gingers know about important changes can save your teammates even if your own Ability/Stamina is recharging.
As stated before, Sprout should mainly focus on finding/gaining Tapes to achieve multiple heals in a run, which can be mainly done by: 
*Scavenging for and using Items on the ground (preferably Common/Uncommon Items)
*Some recommended Items to use to grind Tapes include common Items like a {{II|Stealth Candy|name=false}} or {{II|Gumballs|name=false}}, or Items that speed Machine completion like {{II|Skill Check Candy}}Skill Check Candies, {{II|Jumper Cable|name=false}}s, or {{II|Instructions|name=false}}. However, during Panic Mode, it's safe to use any Items your teammates have left behind for Tapes.

Alongside Sprout's Passive Ability being helpful for reporting danger, if there are no Cosmos or Gingers in the current team, but there's a Bassie, it's better to alert them who needs healing as they can carry heals for heal storing for future Floors where the team gets hurt.

There are many ways Sprout is able to get Tapes:
*Encountering Twisteds;
*Completing Machines;
*Using {{CDI|Penny Pincher/Spare Change|name=true}} cards:
**Using {{CDI|Blind Grab/Lost and Found|name=false}} and {{CDI|Avaricious/Covetous|name=false}} Cards are also slightly more advantageous for Sprout.
*Using [[Items]], especially rarer ones.
{{CI|Ginger|name=true}}, however, is really similar to Sprout, with her Ability being more potent and having average extraction potential at the cost of having low mobility and hurdles in the healing process. If you are playing in a team that can withstand 1 Heart Heals ({{Type|Main}} Toons or a distracting {{CI|Looey|name=true}}) or might need a backup distractor, Sprout would be a better pick, while if the team can handle distracting but are short some extractors and Healers and would be kind enough to help you, Ginger would be good.

Overall, Sprout is really good at on-field healing thanks to his mobility. He can respond to injuries very quickly due to his Passive notifying him. He act somewhat like an ambulance and paramedic in comparison to the other healers.

