*Sprout is the second [[Toon]] to have both their Toon and [[Twisted Sprout|Twisted counterpart]] appear in the game's thumbnail, along with [[Pebble]], with the first being {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}} & [[Blot]], the third being [[Shelly]], the fourth being [[Gourdy]], the fifth being [[Coal]], and the sixth being {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}.
*Sprout is inferred to be left-handed, as seen in his idle animation.
*There is an error in Sprout's (and [[Cosmo]]'s) "Team work" [[Sticker]] where his arms are the same color as his body instead of light red.
*Sprout's [[Savory Charm]] from his idle animation is stored in his body, only taken out when the idle is used.
**This is the same case with other [[Toons]] that carry Items with their model for a certain animation, though Sprout and [[Cosmo]]'s (with the [[Sweet Charm]]) cases are the only ones where a [[Trinket]] is shown during an idle animation. 
*Sprout is the second [[Toon]] to be a plant, (being a strawberry), with the first being [[Dandy]] (a flower), and the third being [[Gourdy]] (a pumpkin).
*Sprout is the only base-game [[Main Character]] [[Toon]] who doesn't have an emotions sheet.
*Sprout has the longest [[Ability]] cooldown, with it being 100 seconds long, tying with [[Ginger]], [[Glisten]], and [[Teagan]].
**Sprout has the longest Ability cooldown for a [[Main Character]].
*Sprout is the only [[Main Character]] whose name doesn't end with a vowel.
*Sprout and [[Ginger]] have many gameplay similarities.
**They both have an [[Ability]] that costs 100 [[Tapes]] to heal other [[Toons]], followed with a 100 second cooldown.
***The cooldown is increased by 30 seconds and the price is increased by 50 Tapes per extra Sprout/Ginger.
**They both have an equal number of Stars in [[Skill Check]] and [[Extraction Speed]].
**They both have one more Star in their [[Stamina]] than their [[Movement Speed]].
***To counter the latter fact, they have an even amount Stars of Movement Speed and an odd amount Stars of Stamina.
